  <data name="ArtifactJournal" xml:space="preserve"><value>The journal is in the $J alternate data stream (ADS) of the $UsnJrnl file. An acquisition tool may export this stream as a separate file named $J or $UsnJrnl-$J.</value></data>
  <data name="ArtifactMft" xml:space="preserve"><value>The master file table identifies files and their parent folders. Use the $MFT from the same volume as $J or $LogFile to look up paths.</value></data>
  <data name="ArtifactLog" xml:space="preserve"><value>This file records NTFS metadata transactions. You can analyze it on its own.</value></data>
  <data name="ArtifactAcquire" xml:space="preserve"><value>For a disk image, use Select files, then choose the volume and artifacts. For an existing extraction, select the files or folder saved by your acquisition tool.</value></data>
  <data name="GuideOpenFiles" xml:space="preserve"><value>In Settings, select files or an extracted folder. When opening one file, review any automatically added companions and use × to remove unwanted ones. Selecting several files uses only those files.</value></data>
  <data name="GuideOpenImage" xml:space="preserve"><value>Open the disk image, check the NTFS volume, artifacts and extraction folder, then choose Extract and analyze. For a logical image, select files present in the acquisition.</value></data>
  <data name="GuideOpenVerify" xml:space="preserve"><value>After analysis, open the extracted files and manifest from Settings to check paths and SHA-256 hashes. Source information in the File menu lists the loaded sources and any parse warnings.</value></data>
  <data name="GuideFollow" xml:space="preserve"><value>Trace a file</value></data>
  <data name="GuideFollowFilter" xml:space="preserve"><value>In All records, search by file name or change reason. Set start and end dates in the date filter. Dates include the whole day unless you enter a time. The filter uses the display time zone from Settings.</value></data>
  <data name="GuideFollowFile" xml:space="preserve"><value>Select a record and press Enter to open the same file and record in File history. If you know the name, you can start in File history. Press Alt+Left to return to your selected row in All records.</value></data>
  <data name="GuideFollowPath" xml:space="preserve"><value>Show full paths to see the recorded location and path source in separate columns. Expand the evidence in Overview to distinguish folders reconstructed from the journal from those inferred using the collected MFT.</value></data>
  <data name="GuideInspect" xml:space="preserve"><value>Inspect source records</value></data>
  <data name="GuideCompare" xml:space="preserve"><value>For a rename or move, use Compare changes to compare names and parent folders. When a change has multiple source rows, each row represents a separate record.</value></data>
  <data name="GuideFields" xml:space="preserve"><value>Select a source row to inspect it in the current tab. Record details shows fields such as FileName and Reason. The JSON tab shows the indexed values in a copyable format. Open Hex to inspect the source bytes.</value></data>
  <data name="GuideHex" xml:space="preserve"><value>Double-click a source row or press Enter to open Hex. Addresses are byte offsets from the start of the extracted file. Select a byte to see its field and decoded value. Drag or use Shift+arrow to select a range, then press Ctrl+C to copy.</value></data>
  <data name="GuideTransactions" xml:space="preserve"><value>Transactions and recovery</value></data>
  <data name="GuideTransactionReads" xml:space="preserve"><value>Open $LogFile and search for a name or hexadecimal LSN. The raw header contains bytes recorded on disk. Redo and Undo offsets start at the beginning of each reconstructed payload.</value></data>
  <data name="GuideRecovery" xml:space="preserve"><value>Open Investigation leads to check the active $J for patterns such as document deletions. Tools can scan raw bytes in the open $J or $LogFile, or in a separate RAW source, for record candidates. Compare each candidate with its source records before attributing it to an event.</value></data>
  <data name="GuideSave" xml:space="preserve"><value>Save results</value></data>
  <data name="GuideExportScope" xml:space="preserve"><value>Export in All records saves matching records across all pages. Export in the file header saves only the selected file’s history. To include reconstructed paths and their sources, choose the corresponding CSV option.</value></data>
  <data name="GuideFolder" xml:space="preserve"><value>Choose the output folder under Analysis options in Settings. You can also choose a destination each time you export a CSV. Open the extraction folder from Settings to inspect saved evidence.</value></data>
